WEBVTT

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:34.880
The principle of Geumgang lies in the firmness of wisdom and virtue force

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:38.640
that is never destroyed despite attack from the outside.

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:41.600
Just as the protector of Buddhism is Buddha,

00:00:41.600 --> 00:00:45.200
Geumgang Yeoksa protects the world from evil.

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:49.920
Geumgang Pumsae embodies the desire to protect justice in the world

00:00:49.920 --> 00:00:54.240
and train the body to become like the splendor of Geumgang Mountain,

00:00:54.240 --> 00:00:58.080
the soul of the Korean peninsula through Taekwondo.

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:00.800
The progress line of Geumgang Pumsae,

00:01:00.800 --> 00:01:03.920
which represents the strong and unshakable warrior,

00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:11.470
is the character San, which means mountain.

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:15.710
We will now take a look at the key moves of Geumgang Pumsae.

00:01:15.710 --> 00:03:04.460
Geumgang Pumsae consists of six key moves, namely

00:03:28.530 --> 00:03:35.280
We will now take a closer look at each of the key moves of Geumgang Pumsae.

00:03:35.280 --> 00:03:38.320
Batang Son Apchigi

00:03:38.320 --> 00:03:42.080
is a technique used to attack a target in a straight line

00:03:42.080 --> 00:03:46.560
using the lower part of the palm of your hand.

00:03:46.560 --> 00:03:51.040
First, tilt your hand outward by 45 degrees.

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:53.920
Then pull your wrist back as much as possible

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:58.580
to concentrate force on the palm of your hand.

00:03:58.580 --> 00:04:00.980
Your hand should be level with your chin

00:04:00.980 --> 00:04:04.020
and aligned with the center line.

00:04:04.020 --> 00:04:06.980
You can concentrate the force on the palm of your hand

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:12.140
when the wrist is tilted 45 degrees outward.

00:04:12.140 --> 00:04:15.260
Sonnal Anmakgi

00:04:15.260 --> 00:04:20.140
is a technique used to perform Anmakgi with the hand blade.

00:04:20.140 --> 00:04:23.740
The hand blade should be level with the solar plexus

00:04:23.740 --> 00:04:28.160
and aligned with the center line.

00:04:28.160 --> 00:04:34.050
Be careful not to let the tip of the hand rise above the shoulder.

00:04:34.130 --> 00:04:37.360
Geumgang Makgi

00:04:37.360 --> 00:04:44.640
is a combination of Olgul Olyo Makgi and Aremakgi performed simultaneously.

00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:48.160
For Aremakgi, the space between your leg and arm

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:51.040
should be about two raised fists.

00:04:51.040 --> 00:04:54.320
The space between the arm blocking the face and forehead

00:04:54.320 --> 00:04:58.540
should be about one raised fist.

00:04:58.540 --> 00:05:01.020
This move must be performed slowly,

00:05:01.020 --> 00:05:06.770
exerting force on the lower abdomen.

00:05:06.770 --> 00:05:09.650
Be careful not to let the arm blocking the face

00:05:09.650 --> 00:05:20.000
cross the elbow blocking the lower body on the outside.

00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:23.180
Geumdol Jogui

00:05:23.180 --> 00:05:26.220
Place the wrist of one arm at the lilac crest

00:05:26.220 --> 00:05:29.820
and the other arm in front of the solar plexus.

00:05:29.820 --> 00:05:32.780
The space between the arm on top and the torso

00:05:32.780 --> 00:05:35.980
should be about one raised fist.

00:05:35.980 --> 00:05:39.180
The fist on top must be placed in the same line

00:05:39.180 --> 00:05:46.660
as the first on the lilac crest.

00:05:46.660 --> 00:05:50.270
Santolmakgi

00:05:50.270 --> 00:05:52.350
is a move to perform techniques

00:05:52.350 --> 00:05:58.270
by utilizing the twist of the lower and upper body.

00:05:58.270 --> 00:06:03.470
One arm is used to block the face inside out with the inner wrist.

00:06:03.470 --> 00:06:09.710
The other arm is used to block the face outside in with the outer wrist.

00:06:09.710 --> 00:06:16.340
The wrists should be level with the philtrum.

00:06:16.340 --> 00:06:18.180
Elbows should face downward

00:06:18.180 --> 00:06:26.060
and made perpendicular to the ground without bending the wrist.

00:06:26.060 --> 00:06:28.940
Hakdari Sange

00:06:29.020 --> 00:06:32.460
is a useful technique to dodge an opponent's attack

00:06:32.460 --> 00:06:37.760
or perform a counter attack after a dodge.

00:06:37.760 --> 00:06:41.200
Maintain balance with one leg.

00:06:41.200 --> 00:06:44.320
Bend and raise the other knee

00:06:44.320 --> 00:06:47.360
and lightly touch the arc of the back of the foot blade

00:06:47.360 --> 00:06:53.630
inside the supporting leg.

00:06:53.630 --> 00:06:58.110
Face forward so your knees don't open outward

00:06:58.110 --> 00:07:00.510
and naturally straighten the ankle of the leg

00:07:00.510 --> 00:07:04.670
inside the knee of the supporting leg.

00:07:04.670 --> 00:07:10.590
Then bend the supporting leg to the same height as Chuchumseogi.

00:07:10.590 --> 00:07:15.390
These are the six key moves of Kumgang Pumsae.

00:07:15.390 --> 00:07:20.590
We will now look at the moves in succession connecting each move.

00:07:20.590 --> 00:07:24.190
The key moves of Kumgang first part consist of

00:07:24.190 --> 00:07:26.510
Anpalmok Hechomakgi

00:07:26.510 --> 00:07:29.390
Oren Patangson Apchigi

00:07:29.470 --> 00:07:32.110
Oren Patangson Apchigi

00:07:32.110 --> 00:07:34.910
Oren Patangson Apchigi

00:07:34.910 --> 00:07:37.310
Oren Sonnal Anmakgi

00:07:37.310 --> 00:07:40.270
Oren Sonnal Anmakgi

00:07:40.270 --> 00:07:45.570
and Oren Sonnal Anmakgi

00:07:45.570 --> 00:07:49.170
When performing Anpalmok Hechomakgi

00:07:49.170 --> 00:07:51.730
cross the left arm outside the right arm

00:07:51.730 --> 00:07:54.530
if the left foot is in front.

00:07:54.530 --> 00:07:57.490
Your fists must not rise above your shoulders

00:07:57.490 --> 00:08:00.770
when blocking defending your torso.

00:08:00.770 --> 00:08:05.170
Your wrist should be level with your solar plexus.

00:08:05.170 --> 00:08:09.970
Kumgang is a Pumsae that expresses mass.

00:08:09.970 --> 00:08:14.050
When connecting Patangson Apchigi and Sonnal Anmakgi

00:08:14.050 --> 00:08:19.780
keep in mind this concept.

00:08:19.780 --> 00:08:21.940
When performing Sonnal Anmakgi

00:08:21.940 --> 00:08:27.680
the foot should set backwards in a straight line.

00:08:27.680 --> 00:08:30.240
Cautions for Kumgang first part

00:08:30.240 --> 00:08:33.280
taking a closer look.

00:08:33.280 --> 00:08:36.000
When performing Anpalmok Hechomakgi

00:08:36.000 --> 00:08:38.080
the two fists should not cross

00:08:38.080 --> 00:08:44.370
and turn from front to inside like Ddeungjungmok Apchigi.

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:46.050
Be careful not to rush

00:08:46.050 --> 00:08:50.370
connecting the three Patangson Apchigi moves.

00:08:50.370 --> 00:08:57.330
Be sure not to let the high knee of the ball foot bend.

00:08:57.330 --> 00:09:01.330
When setting the foot back from Duikubi to Duikubi

00:09:01.330 --> 00:09:05.970
be careful not to let the foot draw a circle as it sets back.

00:09:05.970 --> 00:09:09.170
Set the foot back before the center axis turns

00:09:09.170 --> 00:09:15.100
or the heel of the hind foot twists without moving the center.

00:09:15.100 --> 00:09:17.340
When performing Sonnal Anmakgi

00:09:17.340 --> 00:09:22.940
be careful not to let the elbow move away too far from the torso.

00:09:22.940 --> 00:09:26.140
We will now practice the moves of Kumgang first part

00:09:26.140 --> 00:09:44.590
in succession while watching the video.

00:09:44.590 --> 00:09:46.990
The key moves of Kumgang second part

00:09:46.990 --> 00:09:49.870
consist of

00:09:49.870 --> 00:10:00.750
Kumgangmakgi

00:10:00.750 --> 00:10:04.290
Keuntoljjokui

00:10:04.290 --> 00:10:08.530
Keuntoljjokui

00:10:08.530 --> 00:10:11.410
Sandeulmakgi

00:10:11.410 --> 00:10:14.850
Anpalmok Hechomakgi

00:10:14.850 --> 00:10:25.580
and Arae Hechomakgi.

00:10:25.580 --> 00:10:29.420
When transitioning to Kumgangmakgi from the previous move

00:10:29.420 --> 00:10:31.820
push off the ground with your left foot

00:10:31.820 --> 00:10:34.700
and move your center to your right foot.

00:10:34.700 --> 00:10:37.100
Turn your right foot to the central axis

00:10:37.100 --> 00:10:40.860
and slowly assume the Hakdariseogi posture.

00:10:40.860 --> 00:10:47.360
Hakdariseogi Kumgangmakgi should be performed firmly and slowly.

00:10:47.360 --> 00:10:50.320
Be mindful of the space between the parts of your body

00:10:50.320 --> 00:10:54.860
when assuming the Kumgangmakgi posture.

00:10:54.860 --> 00:10:56.060
For Arae Makgi

00:10:56.060 --> 00:11:01.980
the space between your leg and arm should be about two raised fists.

00:11:01.980 --> 00:11:05.420
The space between the arm blocking the face and forehead

00:11:05.420 --> 00:11:09.100
should be about one raised fist.

00:11:09.100 --> 00:11:13.020
When spinning from Keuntoljjokui to Keuntoljjokui

00:11:13.020 --> 00:11:16.620
the ball of the setting right foot should start at the same line

00:11:16.620 --> 00:11:18.860
with the ball of the left foot.

00:11:18.860 --> 00:11:22.940
Next, move one foot length and spin.

00:11:22.940 --> 00:11:26.940
Switch from Oren Keuntoljjokui to Wen Keuntoljjokui

00:11:26.940 --> 00:11:31.710
then perform Oren Keuntoljjokui again.

00:11:31.710 --> 00:11:34.430
Cautions for Kumgang second part.

00:11:34.430 --> 00:11:38.190
Taking a closer look.

00:11:38.190 --> 00:11:43.760
Be careful not to rush Hakdariseogi.

00:11:43.760 --> 00:11:45.920
When performing Kumgangmakgi

00:11:45.920 --> 00:11:49.280
be careful not to let the arm blocking the face upward

00:11:49.280 --> 00:11:58.190
cross the elbow of the arm blocking the lower body from the outside.

00:11:58.190 --> 00:12:00.430
When performing Keuntoljjokui

00:12:00.430 --> 00:12:05.230
your eyes should not be directed forward.

00:12:05.230 --> 00:12:07.150
Do not jump when spinning

00:12:07.150 --> 00:12:10.830
and be mindful of where you're looking.

00:12:10.830 --> 00:12:12.830
When performing Haejeomakgi

00:12:12.830 --> 00:12:16.030
be careful not to let your fists cross each other

00:12:16.030 --> 00:12:21.180
and spin inward like Deungjumokapchigi.

00:12:21.180 --> 00:12:24.540
We will now practice the moves of Kumgang second part

00:12:24.540 --> 00:12:54.370
in succession while watching the video.

00:12:54.370 --> 00:12:58.450
The key moves of Kumgang third part consist of

00:12:59.330 --> 00:13:02.560
Sandeulmakgi

00:13:02.560 --> 00:13:14.580
Geumgangmakgi

00:13:14.580 --> 00:13:18.210
Geuntoljjokui

00:13:18.210 --> 00:13:19.970
Geuntoljjokui

00:13:19.970 --> 00:13:30.750
Geumgangmakgi

00:13:30.750 --> 00:13:34.020
Geuntoljjokui

00:13:34.020 --> 00:13:37.740
Geuntoljjokui

00:13:37.740 --> 00:13:41.570
Sandeulmakgi

00:13:41.570 --> 00:13:45.010
Anpalmok Haejeomakgi

00:13:45.010 --> 00:13:59.950
and Arae Haejeomakgi.

00:13:59.950 --> 00:14:02.350
For moves that are performed slowly

00:14:02.350 --> 00:14:04.430
complete the foot moves first

00:14:04.430 --> 00:14:08.930
then connect to the hand moves.

00:14:09.090 --> 00:14:12.450
Use one leg to maintain your center.

00:14:12.450 --> 00:14:15.970
Bend and raise the other knee.

00:14:15.970 --> 00:14:19.250
Then lightly touch the arc of the back of the foot blade

00:14:19.250 --> 00:14:22.530
to the inner knee of the supporting leg.

00:14:22.530 --> 00:14:24.290
The knee should face forward

00:14:24.290 --> 00:14:27.090
and the ankle should straighten naturally.

00:14:27.090 --> 00:14:28.850
The knee should face forward

00:14:28.850 --> 00:14:34.300
and maintain posture with the ankle naturally straightened.

00:14:34.300 --> 00:14:37.020
Cautions for Kumgang third part

00:14:37.020 --> 00:14:42.100
taking a closer look.

00:14:42.100 --> 00:14:44.660
Do not drag your foot to bring it to the knee

00:14:44.660 --> 00:14:47.620
when performing Hakdari Seogi.

00:14:47.620 --> 00:14:48.820
When spinning

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:50.340
be careful not to mix the

00:14:50.340 --> 00:14:55.630
Chageun Doljjokui and Geuntoljjokui moves.

00:14:55.630 --> 00:14:59.860
Be careful not to jump when spinning.

00:14:59.860 --> 00:15:02.980
We will now practice the moves of Kumgang third part

00:15:02.980 --> 00:15:48.850
in succession while watching the video.

00:15:48.850 --> 00:15:55.170
The key moves of Kumgang fourth part consist of

00:15:55.170 --> 00:15:58.340
Sandeulmakgi

00:15:58.340 --> 00:16:10.020
Geumgangmakgi

00:16:10.020 --> 00:16:13.500
Geuntoljjokui

00:16:13.500 --> 00:16:17.840
and Geuntoljjokui.

00:16:17.840 --> 00:16:20.880
To let the arm blocking the face cross the elbow

00:16:20.880 --> 00:16:26.860
blocking the lower body on the outside.

00:16:26.860 --> 00:16:29.500
Cautions for Kumgang fourth part

00:16:29.500 --> 00:16:32.820
taking a closer look.

00:16:32.820 --> 00:16:35.220
Be mindful of the direction of your eyes

00:16:35.220 --> 00:16:39.760
when connecting each move.

00:16:39.760 --> 00:16:43.040
We will now practice the moves of Kumgang fourth part

00:16:43.040 --> 00:17:06.210
in succession while watching the video.

00:17:06.210 --> 00:17:14.180
This concludes the training for Kumgang Pumse.

00:17:14.180 --> 00:17:16.500
We will take another look at all the moves

00:17:16.500 --> 00:19:07.500
and master Pumse.

00:19:07.500 --> 00:19:10.540
We have looked at the key moves of Kumgang Pumse

00:19:10.540 --> 00:19:13.500
and provided thorough explanations for each move

00:19:13.500 --> 00:19:16.300
and things to watch out for.

00:19:16.300 --> 00:19:18.060
Train the moves repeatedly

00:19:18.060 --> 00:19:20.300
while reminding yourself of the firmness

00:19:20.300 --> 00:19:24.450
and strength embodied by Kumgang.

00:19:24.450 --> 00:19:25.650
We will see you again

00:19:25.650 --> 00:19:28.050
in the Tebek Pumse video.

00:19:28.050 --> 00:19:29.330
Thanks for watching.

